where SP is the set of arcs in the corresponding shortest path. For example, in the grid network as shown in Figure 2, L(π |s) = R(Sfinal, Afinal) is the total length of the grey arcs.
3.4.3. Policy-based reinforcement learning method Here, we define the policy of the pointer network as p(π |s), and the goal of the policy is to assign high probability to the solution that the corresponding shortest path has large total length and low probability to the solution that with small total length. The policy can be provided by neural network using chain rule. As explained before,

